WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.882
(mystical bell-like music)

00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:33.600
(staccato instrumental music)

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.400
- [Narrator] In the
villages of Guizhou, China,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.612
there is a rich tradition of embroidery.

00:00:37.612 --> 00:00:41.463
But perhaps none is more
intricate than that of the Miao.

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:10.010
(lively dance music)

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.840
- [Narrator] The Miao don't
have a written language.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.780
Instead, they use their embroidery

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.057
to document their history,
legends and culture.

00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:20.390
(lively oriental music)

00:01:43.791 --> 00:01:46.734
(girls laughing)

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:50.670
(soft instrumental music)

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:51.520
- [Narrator] Miao embroidery

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.740
uses incredibly intricate stitching

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.483
and hand-spun threads
to create the designs.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.803
Some garments can take years to complete.

00:02:10.981 --> 00:02:12.610
- [Narrator] Preserving this tradition

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.573
is incredibly important to the Miao.

00:02:28.121 --> 00:02:31.288
(soft rhythmic music)

00:02:33.955 --> 00:02:36.372
(bell tones)

